{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Candidate field occurrence from a cross-source log audit (2026-07-30) — offered as a lead, explicitly NOT as proof.\n\nThis bug describes `materialize/_materialize_tree` being able to lazy-fetch unboundedly on a partial clone with no `run_git` timeout. There is exactly one production event in the retained journald history (2026-07-03 -> today) whose shape matches an unbounded fetch/clone: the review bot's only per-review timeout, on the Gerrit host `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`:\n\n    2026-07-13T08:22:05Z  VOTER_ERROR {\"event\": \"VOTER_ERROR\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1783930925.7817554,\n      \"change_id\": \"I0cbe64257ac6d593dc0e024cfb875c62abcdf611\",\n      \"revision_id\": null, \"vote_value\": null, \"http_status\": null,\n      \"error\": \"review timed out after 1200.0s — abandoned to keep the queue draining\n                (hung clone/subprocess/LLM); the backfill reconciler will retry\"}\n\nRelevant details:\n- It is the ONLY `review timed out after` event in the whole retained journal (verified: `journalctl --since 2026-07-03 | grep -c \"review timed out after\"` = 1), and the last `VOTER_ERROR` of any kind on record.\n- The review hung for the full 1200s ceiling — i.e. it did not fail, it made no progress until the outer watchdog killed it. That is the signature an untimed `run_git` fetch would produce.\n- The bot's own message names \"hung clone\" first among the suspects.\n\nWhat I could NOT establish: the message is a generic catch-all emitted by the outer `asyncio.wait_for` watchdog, so it does not identify which subprocess hung. I have no stack, no git trace, and no evidence tying it to `_materialize_tree` specifically rather than to a subprocess or LLM call. The 1200s watchdog (from 9d7c / 89be) is what caught it, and it self-healed via the backfill reconciler.\n\nUse: if a timeout is added to `run_git` under this ticket, this event is a concrete pre-fix datapoint to cite, and its non-recurrence afterwards would be weak-but-real evidence. Do not treat it as a confirmed reproduction."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785451671066980001,"uuid":"925ef969-542c-43ad-9cca-40532ff34179"}